package mcpbridge

// Every external host uses the same execution and presentation guidance.
const workflowStartInstructions = "For a selected LazyMind Workflow, call workflow.start. Pass known startup answers as clarification_values, not only in request_context. When status is needs_input, no session has been created: ask the returned questions using their exact IDs, merge returned clarification_values with the user's answers, preserve request_context and revision_id, and resubmit with a new idempotency_key because the payload changed. Do not begin steps or open a panel before a session_id is returned. When the task uses source files, include them in start.inputs keyed by the declared external material ID; each value is an ordered array of {local_path} or existing {resource_id, revision, content_hash}. Use the declared startup_contract.input_materials metadata for exact material_id values; never invent input keys. If a key is rejected, correct it using that contract while retaining every selected source. Resolve host attachments to absolute regular-file paths on the Connector machine first. Start imports and binds every supplied file before creating the run; a file name or path mentioned only in request_context is not an input binding. If any selected source cannot be prepared, report the error and do not retry without that source. Keep inputs and legacy input_bindings on different material IDs. "

const workflowExecutionInstructions = "Then call workflow.step.begin for a ready step according to state. When the user asks to continue, read workflow.state first; if stopped, call workflow.session.resume on the same run. A returned execution_id is already scheduled. For user-requested edits to completed artifacts, call workflow.edit.context, follow its original LazyMind Skills with a native worker, and atomically save validated linked artifacts via workflow.edit.commit; do not rewind local edits or scoped page changes. For an explicit workflow rerun, begin an exact projection.rewindable target; for an explicit retry, begin an exact projection.retryable target with retry_origin=user. Claim an existing active execution with workflow.step.claim instead of beginning a duplicate. Execute a step_contract only with an execution_handle; publish each output with workflow.artifact.publish as it is generated, then send only the outcome with workflow.step.complete using that handle unchanged. When executor_host is lazymind, end the current turn and wait for a notification. In external steps, save_artifact/save_artifacts means publish each output immediately (key becomes slot) with a stable positive seq per slot, wait for its acknowledgement, and complete only when execution finishes. Read inputs from step_contract.inputs; resolve references with workflow.artifact.get or workflow.input.get, and use workflow.artifact.list to find an artifact ID by slot key. Follow control.continuation. If control.input_request is present, ask its exact questions using the host question UI or conversation and wait for the actual user reply; save it with workflow.input.answer using the exact artifact_id, revision, state_version and a stable command_id. Never infer answers, treat the launch request as an answer, or approve a review. Answering does not resume a stop or start a step. On awaiting_user without input_request, tell the user to review in the panel and END this turn immediately. Do not approve the review yourself, start another step, or poll while waiting. On awaiting_executor, stopped, completed, or binding_required, also end this turn. Resume only on a new notification or explicit user input, then read workflow.state first. "

const workflowFinishInstructions = "Use a stable idempotency_key for unchanged-payload start retries; use a new key when answers or inputs change. Report completion only when workflow.state confirms completed, then deliver artifact links from workflow.artifact.list."

const workflowHostInstructions = "The host displays the Workflow panel automatically for the bound conversation after session creation. Review and control the Workflow in that panel. Do not open a browser panel or include a panel link in your reply. Use an explicit unique idempotency_key of 16–256 characters and preserve it with the returned session_id on unchanged-payload retries. Native conversation identity belongs to the host connector; never guess an ID or use the Workflow session_id as driver_session_id. If the host reports missing identity, follow its returned connection guidance and retry the same start. "

const workflowExternalInstructions = "For step_contract.external_execution.version=1, the bound root controller holds the execution_handle and all Workflow state-writing tools. Delegate generation and validation to native host subagents using the complete pinned step_contract.prompt, execution.skill_files, execution.constraints, acceptance criteria, typed inputs and required outputs. Native and external executors use this same business contract; external_execution.adapter_instructions only maps execution capabilities. Legacy revisions without execution retain their pinned external_execution contract. Do not give workers the execution_handle, credentials, or permission to begin, publish or complete steps. Workers return a typed artifact manifest and validation evidence; the root publishes acknowledged outputs and completes with executor_ref identifying the worker. Root proxies declared package/global tools through workflow.tool.list and workflow.tool.call, preserving command_id on unchanged retries. Do not execute native-only scripts or call model.chat to replace a worker. Read every supplied LazyMind Skill before work; these Skills are the authoritative business instructions. Never substitute host domain Skills or an independent workflow; host helpers only implement tool operations. Discover LazyMind tools first and use an applicable configured tool; use host tools when LazyMind lacks the required operation. Missing Skill content must be obtained from the pinned revision or reported, never guessed. Include used Skill paths and tool substitutions in worker validation evidence. If neither is available, explain what to configure in LazyMind and yield so the same run can be retried. Resolve file inputs on the actual execution machine; paths returned by another machine are not local paths. On stop, cancel owned workers where supported; never publish stale results after the execution grant is revoked. "

const workflowActionInstructions = "For an artifact_edit notification, use workflow.action.get and workflow.action.respond, not step.begin or rewind. Delegate each exact LazyMind generation_request to a native worker; the shared planner validates the response and builds a preview. When ready or cancelled, end the turn: only the user confirms the preview in LazyMind. This works even after the Workflow is completed. "

const workflowInstructions = workflowActionInstructions + workflowStartInstructions + workflowHostInstructions + workflowExecutionInstructions + workflowExternalInstructions + workflowFinishInstructions
